  "body": "[CSSOM spec](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#dom-cssstyledeclaration-_dashed_attribute) describes about identifiers with leading dashs, but they conflict with current WebIDL spec, because now we allow `/_?[A-Za-z][0-9A-Z_a-z-]*/` in identifiers.\r\n\r\nSo I'd suggest to update the pattern to allow a hypen as a leading character to make both specs consistent with each other. Specifically, I suggest following two candidates.\r\n- `[_-]?[A-Za-z][0-9A-Z_a-z-]*`\r\n- `_?[A-Za-z-][0-9A-Z_a-z-]*`\r\n\r\n\r\n",
